          "pseudo_id": "p1",
          "pseudo": "It was foreordained that the ancient epic, long sung by one tribe, would be recast. The director, a weaver of dreams, appointed a daughter of a distant shore to embody the face that launched a thousand ships. Thus was the old shrine shaken; a great clamor rose from the digital agora, where voices cried of theft and of erasure, as if the very stones of Troy had been moved. The contest was not for a role, but for the soul of the story itself, and in the fray, the epic was reborn as a mirror held before the age.",
