          "pseudo_id": "p2",
          "pseudo": "No one remembers the intern who accidentally sent the test email. In the early stages of pre-production for Nolan's adaptation, a junior assistant was tasked with distributing a preliminary casting breakdown document to the core team. She composed the email, attached the file, but then paused to fix a typo in the subject line. In that two-second window, her phone buzzed with a personal message, causing her finger to tap 'Send' prematurely. The email went out to the entire broader development list, including publicists and external consultants, one full week before the official announcement was scheduled. This premature leak, a consequence of a single misplaced finger, ignited the first spark of online speculation and reaction.",
          "source": {
