        {
          "pseudo_id": "p3",
          "pseudo": "If not for a single misheard word in a crowded café, the whole controversy might have been a footnote. The actor who was initially the frontrunner for the role was having lunch near the production office. He thought he overheard a producer say 'we're going another direction.' In reality, the producer had said 'we're going over the costume directions.' This mishearing prompted the actor's agent to aggressively push for a contract extension, creating a momentary contractual standoff. This delay, lasting just forty-eight hours, gave Christopher Nolan's team the pause they needed to reconsider the entire thematic framing of the character.",
